## A note on the code templates

The text above is the MIT License, unmodified. This note does not alter it; it
records the author's intent so that adopters need not guess.

These skills exist to be copied from. The code templates they carry — a
repository adapter, a router file, a settings class, a test module — are
written to be pasted into your own project and edited until they fit.

Copying a template into your own code requires **no attribution** and imposes
**no obligation** on the code you write around it. The templates are yours to
use, in open-source or proprietary work, without notice, credit, or any
requirement to publish what you build.

The attribution clause above applies to redistributing the skill catalogue
itself — forking it, republishing it, or shipping it inside another plugin or
product — not to the code a reader writes after reading it.
